#!/usr/bin/python3
# System Python on purpose: `env python3` can resolve to a mise shim, which adds the mise exec
# env (CARGO_HOME, RUSTUP_*). hcom treats CARGO_* as a contaminated parent and replaces the
# PATH of launched agents with one rebuilt from a clean login shell (no mise shims).
"""hcom-gui: catalog agents and live instances in one table, with buttons that run hcom.

The GUI holds no hcom logic: the table comes from `hcom agent list --all --json` and
`hcom list --json`; every button runs an existing command and logs its output.

Optional ~/.hcom/gui.json:
  {"refresh_seconds": 5,
   "open_with": [{"label": "Zed", "cmd": ["zed", "{dir}"], "key": "z"},
                 {"label": "gitg", "cmd": ["gitg"], "cwd": "{dir}"},
                 {"label": "Backlog", "cmd": ["x-terminal-emulator", "backlog", "board"], "cwd": "{dir}",
                  "if_exists": "{dir}/backlog"}],
   "commands": [{"label": "Kill persistent", "cmd": ["hcom", "kill", "@persistent"], "confirm": true}],
   "columns": ["agent", "instance", "status", "context", "git"],
   "attach": {"herdr": ["sh", "-c", "hcom agent attach \"$1\" && wmctrl -x -a herdr.herdr", "_", "{instance}"]}}
"attach" maps the terminal an instance runs in (Where column) to the Attach command;
other terminals run DEFAULT_ATTACH.
"commands" run as written, without a selected row (optional: confirm, cwd, key).
The toolbar buttons wrap into as many rows as the window width needs; "toolbar_breaks" (button
labels without key or "…"/"▾", e.g. ["Kill group", "Columns"]) also starts a new row after each named button.
"key" (any button) is a Tk event sequence bound in the table, e.g. "z" or "<F2>", shown
in the button label ("Zed (z)").
"open_with" programs also start while an hcom command runs; a quick non-zero exit is logged.
"stats_seconds" (default 60) is how often the usage columns reload life and message events.
"idle_seconds" (default 10): once an instance has been listening this long, the Idle column gets
its class from contrib/idle-classifier/idle_check.py (needs_user, waiting, done; "-" none), once per
listening period. Remote instances report no listening age: they count from the GUI's first sight.
A needs_user row is highlighted in blue, less loudly than a blocked one. Right-click on a classified
row corrects its class (idle_check.py --label, shown with ✓).
"columns" selects and orders the table columns (keys of COLUMNS; default: all); a choice
made with the Columns… button is kept in gui-state.json and takes precedence (Reset drops it);
a column added to hcom-gui after that choice is shown in its default place.
Status columns: each [[status_column]] of hcom config.toml (`hcom agent list --status`) is a column
with key "status:<name>", titled <name>, holding the row's value on one line; a row without a
running instance shows its agent's most recently updated instance. A status column no longer
configured in hcom is dropped from "columns" and the saved choice.
Heading clicks cycle the sort: ascending, descending, default; Empty last (on by default) puts
rows with an empty cell in the sort column last in both directions. The Filter field matches
agent, instance, dir and groups (case-insensitive).
A disabled catalog agent's row is struck through; Hide disabled (on by default) hides it.
Hide non-persistent hides instances without a catalog agent. The toolbar counts the shown rows.
Start: the empty Name field gets "<agent>__" on focus; left unchanged it counts as empty.
Model and reasoning are prefilled from the catalog; only a changed value is passed.
A bar under the Screen tab holds Inject, which types a text into the selected instance's terminal
(`hcom term inject`), with Enter when its checkbox (checked by default) is on, and key buttons
Esc, arrows, Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, 1, 2, 3 that send that key alone. "screen_bar" picks and orders
the bar buttons: a built-in label, or {"label": "y", "keys": "y"} for a button that injects keys
alone; an unknown or invalid item is logged and skipped.
The bottom panel has tabs Screen (`hcom term <instance>`), Transcript (`hcom transcript <instance>`),
Events (`hcom events --agent <instance> --last 50`, one line per event) for the selected row's
running instance, Log (command output and errors) and Report, opened with F5, F6, F7, F8, F9;
Ctrl+R refreshes. Report is a key-value table of the selected row: column title, then the full
value in an aligned column (wrapped lines hang under it; status values with their age). By default
it lists every column, those shown in the table first in table order, then the rest; "report"
(column keys like "columns") shows exactly those in that order.
The open agent tab reloads in the background on selection change and every refresh; it stays at the
end unless scrolled away. A new ERROR log line while another tab is open puts a red dot on the Log tab; opening Log clears it.
Window layout, bottom tab, columns, sort, Empty last and filters (Running only, Blocked only, Hide disabled,
Hide non-persistent) are kept in ~/.hcom/gui-state.json.
"""

